{{Split|Eternity Milestones|Animals|Eternity Challenges}}
{{Split|Supernova|Dilation|Dilation Tree}}

'''{{Keyword|eternity|Eternity}}''' {{Icon|icon tab etern|size=20px}} is the 2nd major reset layer in Revolution Idle, and is the 4th reset layer overall.

=='''Eternity'''==
Upon having {{Keyword|ip|~1.79e308 IP}} (2^1024 IP), an option to {{Keyword|eternity|Eternate}} for {{Keyword|ep|Eternity Points}} ({{Keyword|ep|EP}}) will be displayed.

When the player {{Keyword|eternity|Eternates}}, they will gain {{Keyword|ep|EP}} and {{Keyword|eternity|Eternities}} (Σ), and the following are reset:

# [[Infinity#Infinity Upgrades|{{Keyword|inf|Infinity Upgrades}}]]
# Bought [[Infinity#Generators|Generators]]
# [[Infinity#Infinity Challenges|{{Keyword|inf|Infinity Challenge}}]] completions, their fastest completion times and challenges time sum
# Fastest [[Infinity|{{Keyword|inf|Infinity}}]]
# [[Infinity#Stars|Stars]] and [[Infinity#Stars|Star Upgrades]]
# Everything that [[Infinity|{{Keyword|inf|Infinity}}]] also resets

By default, only 1 {{Keyword|ep|EP}} and 1 {{Keyword|eternity|Eternity}} will be gained upon {{Keyword|eternity|Eternating}}. It is only possible to get more {{Keyword|ep|EP}} per {{Keyword|eternity|Eternate}} after reaching [[Eternity#Eternity_Milestones|Eternity Milestone]] 10 aka "[[Eternity#Eternity_Milestones|Break Eternity]]". Gaining more than 1 {{Keyword|eternity|Eternity}} per {{Keyword|eternity|Eternation}} is only possible after the player has [[Unity|{{Keyword|unity|United}}]] for the first time.

{{Keyword|ep|EP}} is a resource which can be spent on [[Eternity#Animals|{{Keyword|ap|Animal Points}}]] ([[Eternity#Eternity_Milestones|Eternity Milestone]] 3) and [[Eternity#Laboratory|Lab Upgrades]] ([[Eternity#Animals_Milestones|Animals Milestone]] 3). {{Keyword|ep|EP}} is initially limited to {{Keyword|ep|1.08e2466 EP}}, and this amount is required for '''[[Unity|{{Keyword|unity|Unity}}]]''', the next major reset layer.

{{Keyword|eternity|Eternities}} are a resource which are not spent, much like [[Infinity|{{Keyword|inf|Infinities}}]] (∞) in the [[Infinity|{{Keyword|inf|Infinity}}]] layer. Some effects in the game are improved by having more {{Keyword|eternity|Eternities}}, and [[Eternity#Eternity_Milestones|Eternity Milestones]] are reached when the player obtains certain amounts of them.

=='''Eternity Milestones'''==
Eternity Milestones is the 1st {{Keyword|eternity|Eternity}} tab, unlocked by reaching {{Keyword|eternity|Eternity}} for the first time. This tab includes [[Eternity#Eternity_Bonuses|Eternity Bonuses]].

Eternity Milestones are obtained by reaching a certain number of {{Keyword|eternity|Eternities}} (Σ). These milestones unlock automation and new mechanics, modify existing mechanics, and provide boosts, as follows:
# Have 1 Σ : Unlocks Eternity Milestones
# Have 2 Σ : Starting from this {{Keyword|eternity|Eternity|}}, keeps all [[Automations|{{Keyword|auto|Automations}}]]
# [[File:Eternity milestones.png|thumb|Eternity Milestones]]Have 3 Σ : Unlocks Eternity Zoo (see [[Eternity#Animals|Animals]])
# Have 5 Σ : Buying [[Revolution|Revolutions]] (colors) no longer take away [[Revolution#Score|Score]]
# Have 7 Σ : Unlocks [[Automations#IP_Adjuster|{{Keyword|auto|Auto IP Adjuster}}]]
# Have 8 Σ : Unlocks [[Eternity#Eternity_Challenges|Eternity Challenges]]
# Have 12 Σ : Unlocks [[Automations#Autobuy_Infinity_Tree|{{Keyword|auto|Automation for Infinity Upgrades}}]]
# Have 14 Σ : Unlocks [[Automations#Autobuy_Generators|{{Keyword|auto|Automation for Generators}}]]
# Have 16 Σ : Unlocks [[Automations#Autobuy_Stars|{{Keyword|auto|Automation for Stars and Star/Stardust upgrades}}]] and [[Automations#Auto_Eternity|{{Keyword|auto|Auto Eternity}}]]
# Have 32 Σ : "Breaks Eternity" ([[Infinity|{{Keyword|ip|IP}}]] is no longer limited to {{Keyword|ip|~1.79e308 IP}} [2^1024 IP])
# Have 100 Σ : x1.05 to [[Infinity|{{Keyword|ip|IP}}]] gain for each {{Keyword|eternity|Eternity}} (softcapped at 1,000 Σ)

At 32 Σ, the player will Break Eternity ([[Achievements|{{Keyword|ach|Ach. 80}}]]), which removes the [[Infinity|{{Keyword|ip|IP}}]] limit of {{Keyword|ip|~1.79e308 IP}} (2^1024 IP). Reaching higher [[Infinity|{{Keyword|ip|IP}}]] values will reward more {{Keyword|ep|EP}} per {{Keyword|eternity|Eternity}}.

=='''Eternity Bonuses'''==
There are 6 different {{Keyword|eternity|Eternity bonuses}}, as follows:
* Mult gain (starts at x2)
* Lap speed (starts at x2)
* Ascension Power (starts at x1.1)
* Infinity gain (starts at x2)
* Generators power (starts at x2.14)
* Stardust gain (starts at x10)  
{{Keyword|eternity|Eternity bonuses}} improve based on the number of {{Keyword|eternity|Eternities}} (Σ) the player has.

=='''Animals'''==
Animals is the 2nd {{Keyword|eternity|Eternity}} tab, unlocked by reaching [[Eternity#Eternity_Milestones|Eternity Milestone]] 3 (3 Σ). Here, the player can purchase {{Keyword|ap|Animal Points}} ({{Keyword|ap|AP}}) and Animals in the Eternity Zoo. [[Eternity#Animals_Milestones|Animals Milestones]] are now also unlocked (a new sub-tab in the Milestones tab).

==='''AP and Animals'''===
{{Keyword|ap|AP}} is a resource that can be bought with {{Keyword|ep|EP}}, [[Infinity|{{Keyword|ip|IP}}]] and [[Revolution#Score|Score]]. The cost to buy {{Keyword|ap|AP}} will increase with each purchase (individually for each resource).

Animals are bought with {{Keyword|ap|AP}} and will provide the player with many different bonuses that persist through {{Keyword|eternity|Eternities}}.
[[File:Animals.png|thumb|The Animals tab]]
You can "respec" your Animals at any time by using the button (two arrows, forming a circle) within the tab, which will:

* Return you to having no Animals bought
* Return all of your spent {{Keyword|ap|AP}} to you
* Reset your ''current'' {{Keyword|eternity|Eternity}}

There are 81 different Animals and a total of {{Keyword|ap|1,524 AP}} is required to buy them all.

For details on individual Animal costs and bonuses, see the table below:
{{AnimalGrid||true}}

==='''Animals Milestones'''===

Animals Milestones are obtained based on how many Animals the player owns.
They unlock new mechanics, modify existing mechanics and provide bonuses to the player, as follows:

# Own 1 Animal: Unlocks [[Eternity#Slowdown|Slowdown]]
# Own 4 Animals: Unlocks [[Automations#Auto_Slowdown|{{Keyword|auto|Auto Slowdown}}]]
# Own 7 Animals: Unlocks [[Eternity#Laboratory|{{Keyword|rp|Lab}}]]
# Own 10 Animals: [[Revolution#Promote|Promoting]] now resets nothing
# Own 20 Animals: Gain 100% of the {{Keyword|ip|IP}} you would get on [[Infinity|{{Keyword|inf|Infinity}}]], every second. ''Needs [[Eternity#Eternity_Challenges|Eternity Challenges Milestone]] 4 (10 {{Keyword|eternity|EC}} completions) to work fully.''
# Own 48 Animals: +10 free levels to all [[Eternity#Laboratory|{{Keyword|rp|RP}}]] upgrades
# Own 81 Animals: Unlocks [[Eternity#Dilation_&_Dilation Tree|{{Keyword|dilation|Dilation}}]]

==='''Slowdown''' ===

Slowdown is a new mechanic unlocked after the player buys their first Animal and reaches Animals Milestone 1. This mechanic allows the player to exchange lap speed (divides lap speed by 10) for bonus ascensions (+1 [[Revolution#Ascension|Ascension]] to all [[Revolution#Circles|colors]]).

''Note: This is generally a very good trade, but too many Slowdowns can actually decelerate progress by making the first [[Revolution]] take a long time to complete after [[Revolution#Prestige|Prestige]]/[[Revolution#Promote|Promote]].''

The Slowdown menu is displayed by clicking on the Slowdown button located at the bottom-left of the [[Revolution]] page.

When all colors' laps per second (Laps/s) are greater than 10, the player can click the Slowdown button within the menu to gain a Slowdown. Slowdown can also be undone at any time by clicking the Speedup button within the menu.

Slowdown is reset to 0 on [[Infinity|{{Keyword|inf|Infinity}}]] (and by extension, also on {{Keyword|eternity|Eternity}} and [[Unity|{{Keyword|unity|Unity}}]]).

After the player owns 4 Animals, they will reach Animals Milestone 2 and unlock [[Automations#Auto_Slowdown|{{Keyword|auto|Auto Slowdown}}]], which can be used to {{Keyword|auto|automate}} Slowdown. This is done by setting a Laps/s value which all colors must be greater than before a Slowdown is triggered.

When the player reaches both Animals Milestone 4 (own 10 Animals) and [[Eternity#Eternity_Challenges_Milestones|Eternity Challenges Milestone]] 2 (5 {{Keyword|eternity|EC}} completions), having too many Slowdowns is no longer a problem, since they no longer reset anything when they [[Revolution#Promote|Promote]] and [[Revolution#Prestige|Prestige]] (respectively). As such, [[Automations#Auto_Slowdown|{{Keyword|auto|Auto Slowdown}}]] can be set to 10 from now on, in order to achieve the maximum possible Slowdown.

=='''Laboratory'''==
The Laboratory (Lab) is the fourth {{Keyword|eternity|Eternity}} tab, unlocked by reaching [[Eternity#Animals_Milestones|Animals Milestone]] 3 (own 7 [[Eternity#Animals|Animals]]).

The Lab allows the player to get Laboratory Points (LP), by purchasing 3 different upgrades which cost {{Keyword|ep|EP}}:

* Base (+0.20 per level)
* Mult (+0.50 per level)
* Power (+0.01 per level)

The formula for LP/s is:  (Base x Mult) ^ Power

When enough LP has been generated to fill the flask on the right-hand side of the Laboratory page, the Lab level will increase and the player will gain a {{Keyword|rp|Research Point}} ({{Keyword|rp|RP}}).

{{Keyword|rp|RP}} can be used to upgrade 6 different Lab upgrades, as follows:

# [[Infinity|{{Keyword|ip|IP}}]] Gain (x4 per level)
# [[Revolution#Ascension|Ascend Power]] (*(1 + n*0.25) ''where n is level'')
# [[Infinity#Stars|Star Base Mult]] (*(1 + n*0.15))
# {{Keyword|ep|EP}} Gain (*(1 + n*0.5))
# [[Infinity#Generators|Gen. Power Exponent]] (+0.02 per level)
# Common Exponent (+0.01 per level, softcapped at level 500)

Each spent {{Keyword|rp|RP}} will increase a Lab upgrade by one level. Lab upgrades can be respecced at any time, removing all levels and refunding all {{Keyword|rp|RP}} to the player, at the cost of starting a new {{Keyword|eternity|Eternity}}.

=='''Eternity Challenges'''==
Eternity Challenges (EC) is the third {{Keyword|eternity|Eternity}} tab, unlocked by reaching [[Eternity#Eternity_Milestones|Eternity Milestone]] 6 (have 8 Σ). There are 10 Eternity challenges, each with their own unique penalty (similar to [[Infinity#Infinity_Challenges|Infinity Challenges]]), with the goal being to reach the specified target [[Revolution#Score|Score]] under those penalties.

* Unlike Infinity Challenges, where there is the time to complete, each EC initially has 5 difficulties to complete, and every difficulty of an EC will increase the penalties and/or raise the target Score. 
* After completing Insane Trial 4, a 6th difficulty will be available to complete. Each EC difficulty is considered to be an individual challenge by the game, meaning there are a total of 60 ECs.

Completing an EC will award the player 1 free AP, and an extra magnet chance multiplier for each clear beyond 50. Each EC (after the first) is unlocked by completing difficulty 2 of the previous EC.

