== '''Dilation Tree''' ==
{{Keyword|dtp|Dilation Tree}} is the seventh and final {{Keyword|eternity|Eternity}} tab, unlocked by completion of all 50 [[Eternity#Eternity_Challenges|Eternity Challenges]].

[[File:Dilation Tree Numbered.png|alt=The Dilation Tree with Upgrades numbered. The Tree branches from a Center into 3, 4-long, branches. The upgrades in said branches must be bought in order. The numbers are meant to illustrate that order :)|thumb|Dilation Tree]]

Dilation Tree Points ({{Keyword|dtp|DTP}}) can be purchased by using the "Buy DTP" button within the tab, at the cost of {{Keyword|dp|DP}}. The player can allocate {{Keyword|dtp|DTP}} to 13 different Dilation Tree Upgrades (DTU), each providing different bonuses.

The tree works like a classic skill tree, in the sense that the player must buy the upgrades in order ''(see image/below for clarification)''.

''Note: only 1 {{Keyword|dtp|DTP}} needs be allocated to a preceding DTU in order to be able to allocate {{Keyword|dtp|DTP}} to the next DTU (e.g., if 1 {{Keyword|dtp|DTP}} is allocated to CENTER-1, the player can then allocate {{Keyword|dtp|DTP}} to TOP-1, MIDDLE-1 and BOTTOM-1).''

==='''Dilation Tree Upgrades (DTU)'''===
The green tile is the Center Upgrade (CENTER-1), and each branch (aka "Axis") is also colored: Red for Top, Yellow for Middle, and Blue for Bottom. Each axis contains 4 DTU (labelled e.g. for Top: TOP-1, TOP-2, TOP-3 & TOP-4).

Each level of a DTU costs 1 {{Keyword|dtp|DTP}} to buy and each DTU can be bought up to 5 times. A total of 65 {{Keyword|dtp|DTP}} are required to max all DTU.

