Index 4 DTU effects (TOP-4, MIDDLE-4 and BOTTOM-4) can be made 30% stronger by completing both [[Achievements|{{Keyword|ach|Ach. 29}}]] and [[Achievements|{{Keyword|ach|Ach. 140}}]].

''Note: It is highly recommended to complete [[Achievements|{{Keyword|ach|Ach. 29}}]] at {{Keyword|dtp|DTP}} 13, immediately after completing [[Achievements|{{Keyword|ach|Ach. 140}}]] (if you have not done so already). The bonus (detailed above) is very important; without it you will not be able to progress past DTP 16.

When the player wishes to allocate their {{Keyword|dtp|DTP}} in a different way, they can use the button (two arrows, forming a circle) within the tab to "Respec". Respeccing {{Keyword|dtp|DTP}} will:

* Reset your current {{Keyword|eternity|Eternity}}
* Reset (zero) your {{Keyword|dp|Dilation Points}} ({{Keyword|dp|DP}})
* Reset your maximum Dilation Score (to zero)

''Note: The respec penalties may seem harsh, but with limited {{Keyword|dtp|DTP}} it will be necessary to respec often in order to progress through Dilation Tree, using different setups for different purposes. More details on when and why to respec can be found in the [[Walkthrough]].''

==='''Dilation Tree Loadouts'''===
Dilation Tree setups can be saved as "loadouts" by using the button (a dot followed by a line, stacked three high) within the tab. By default, 3 Loadouts can be saved, and 5 additional Loadouts can be purchased for {{Keyword|soul|Souls}} {{Icon|souls}} (starting at {{Keyword|soul|1,000 Souls}} and increasing in cost with each purchase).

Loadouts can be used to quickly switch between commonly used setups, but note this will have the same effect as respeccing {{Keyword|dtp|DTP}} (see previous section for more details).

Players can Export their loadouts to their device's clipboard from within the loadout menu, in the format: Cx;Tx,x,x,x;Mx,x,x,x;Bx,x,x,x. In this expression, C, T, M and B are the initials of the upgrade branches, and each x denotes the level of each upgrade, written in Index order. This format can also be used to Import loadouts from the clipboard.

=== Optimized DT loadouts can be found in the [[Walkthrough]] section. ===

